/*
 * zakpay4.mjs
 *
 * Pay Now, inside the COD confirmation itself - and the rupee sign fixed
 * everywhere it was doubling up.
 *
 * 1. cod_confirmed carries the saving in {{5}} and a Pay Now button. The
 *    button can only vary the last part of its URL, and Meta will not take
 *    %, # or $ there, so it carries the order's own id; /apps/track/pay/<id>
 *    turns that into the real cart link - same items, pay-online code, and
 *    one attribute naming the COD order it replaces. When the new order is
 *    paid, orders/paid cancels the COD twin so nothing is packed twice.
 *
 * 2. money() was sending "INR 1,794" into template slots that already have
 *    a rupee sign typed in front of them, so phones showed "Rs.INR 1,794".
 *    Every template variable now carries the bare number - the saving in
 *    {{5}} included - and money() keeps the symbol for the pages. Paise
 *    survive only when there are any: 1794.2 reads 1,794.20, not 1,794.2.
 *
 * 3. whatsapp.server addresses a button parameter by index, so a template
 *    holding both Pay Now and Track order sends each link to its own button.
 *
 * Every file it touches is copied to ..\\zak-bak first, and a file that is
 * not the version this script was built against is left alone and named.
 * Run it from the repo root.
 */

